ss=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the Tell that said you can take Dalu form means you risk Kuruth - whether this is Wasu-or-Basu-im remains to be seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T05:58:46-07:00","id":135283,"title":"","content":"I hope my question about the First Tongue terms went through. I left a comment asking about some of the etymologies; going to add the new terms to my dictionary when I repost/rewrite it. Does anyone know if comments are moderated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T06:09:26-07:00","id":135287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135281#post135281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that the Tell that said you can take Dalu form means you risk Kuruth - whether this is Wasu-or-Basu-im remains to be seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume Talle letting you take Dalu form should triggers Wasu-Im. But if you not control, you end in Basu-Im in Dalu form. Dalu is partial war-form, so I would think that this softer rage is very appropiate to it, showing that character need to fight, but has control on with whom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-13-2014, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T06:14:15-07:00","id":135291,"title":"","content":"I like that Death Rage is no longer a binary state of being, but why not go all the way and make Rage its own trait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T07:08:47-07:00","id":135318,"title":"","content":"How Rage is trait? It's more two complex Conditions now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T07:34:02-07:00","id":135328,"title":"","content":"Because it's predominantly a state of being?<br /> <br /> Man alive, do I <i>love</i> these rules. Barring a way to possibly avert it in Wasu-Im, this neatly just hits werewolf mythos perfectly, and yet it still feels distinctly Forsaken rather generically werewolf-y. It's sharp as hell, and I think it kicks ass.<br /> <br /> And now all those details from shapechanging make sense, so I'm retroactively pleased with that as well, more than I was.<br /> <br /> Good times are a-coming, dressed in liquid red and velvet dread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T07:35:22-07:00","id":135331,"title":"","content":"I don't like Rage as a trait, myself - it feels too WtA to me (and it never really made sense to me there either.) I am intrigued as to what Primal Urge means now, though - from my understanding, post-IC Harmony kind of measures what the old Primal Urge was - closeness to your spiritual side.<br /> <br /> I'm also interested to see how the personal Kuruth triggers are determined. Will they be chosen by the player, like Integrity Breakpoints for mortals? And on that note, will players get to choose their Harmony Breakpoints, too?<br /> <br /> SO MANY QUESTIONS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T07:40:04-07:00","id":135334,"title":"","content":"My group are not really werewolf gamers but I am very tempted to use a death raging pack on my Promethean throng at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2504-fallen-seraph","name":"Fallen Seraph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T07:48:39-07:00","id":135356,"title":"","content":"Looks like I might be in the minority here, but I'm not liking what I am seeing here. If the smell of fresh meat can set them off, then they can't even walk thru the butcher's section of the grocery store without losing it. It pushes the werewolves into being reclusive, woods-dwellers who can't ever go near civilization.<br /> <br /> Like so many other things, I need to see it in play. Without the Harmony scale, it's hard to gauge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T07:53:18-07:00","id":135363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135356#post135356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like I might be in the minority here, but I'm not liking what I am seeing here. If the smell of fresh meat can set them off, then they can't even walk thru the butcher's section of the grocery store without losing it. It pushes the werewolves into being reclusive, woods-dwellers who can't ever go near civilization.<br /> <br /> Like so many other things, I need to see it in play. Without the Harmony scale, it's hard to gauge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed; without details about how to stop those rages either, games would get old after the 3rd or 4th massacre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T08:14:15-07:00","id":135373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135291#post135291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that Death Rage is no longer a binary state of being, but why not go all the way and make Rage its own trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it's about the bookkeeping. At any given time, especially in GMC, you're keeping track of several different traits and what level they're at (or Aspirations or whatever). If there's an easy and elegant way to get the same point across without adding another trait to keep track of, why not take it? <br /> <br /> I think this fits said bill rather perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T08:23:41-07:00","id":135378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135356#post135356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like I might be in the minority here, but I'm not liking what I am seeing here. If the smell of fresh meat can set them off, then they can't even walk thru the butcher's section of the grocery store without losing it. It pushes the werewolves into being reclusive, woods-dwellers who can't ever go near civilization. Like so many other things, I need to see it in play. Without the Harmony scale, it's hard to gauge.</div> </div> </div> </div> I assume that at reasonably balanced Harmony this won't be a huge issue, but I agree it will be important to see what the triggers are at what Harmony levels to know for sure. The Kuruth mechanics themselves I like, but depending on how easy it is to trigger it might make it too difficult to actually play a werewolf character who isn't a complete lose canon. Hopefully we'll find out in a future preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:32:03-07:00","id":135424,"title":"","content":"I'm really not digging the infectious Basu-Im thing. There's nothing fun about the entire troupe losing control of their characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:37:24-07:00","id":135429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135424#post135424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really not digging the infectious Basu-Im thing. There's nothing fun about the entire troupe losing control of their characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:38:15-07:00","id":135430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135424#post135424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really not digging the infectious Basu-Im thing. There's nothing fun about the entire troupe losing control of their characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure they still for the most part control their characters, unless the ST says otherwise. It likely functions much like Frenzy and will have a sidebar or just handwave that the players are still in control, but have certain guidelines in which they should act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:47:10-07:00","id":135443,"title":"","content":"I'm not thrilled with the implication that non werewolf pack members are considered fair game in a mass frenzy though, what's the point of allowing wolfblooded and even muggles into a pack if they're just going to get murdered the first time their packmates lose their temper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:55:56-07:00","id":135448,"title":"","content":"Don't forget Elodoths can quell Kuruth to prevent a potential disaster if they really need to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:15:22-07:00","id":135455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135356#post135356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like I might be in the minority here, but I'm not liking what I am seeing here. If the smell of fresh meat can set them off, then they can't even walk thru the butcher's section of the grocery store without losing it. It pushes the werewolves into being reclusive, woods-dwellers who can't ever go near civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, Monroe on Grimm seems to manage just fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:16:23-07:00","id":135456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135443#post135443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not thrilled with the implication that non werewolf pack members are considered fair game in a mass frenzy though, what's the point of allowing wolfblooded and even muggles into a pack if they're just going to get murdered the first time their packmates lose their temper?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you aren't supposed to take them hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:25:07-07:00","id":135492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135455#post135455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, Monroe on Grimm seems to manage just fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but he's gone to great lengths to be more in control than his Blutbaden sub-species. He's <i>vegetarian</i>, for goodness sake. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:26:47-07:00","id":135494,"title":"","content":"I'll also point out that if the whole PC group goes into Basu-im, then you can just time skip forward.<br /> <br /> I think this was, in part, to address the issue at the start of the preview: one PC going into Kuruth and everyone else having to deal with it. If you can't stop them while in Wasu-im, while they are still in relative control and can contribute more effectively, then they go into Basu-im and drag everyone with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:38:28-07:00","id":135510,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, since you forget everything you did in Basu-Im anyway, you can cut to the pack waking up 12 hours later. If you don't want to deal with it beyond that, you can leave it at &quot;you don't know what happened, but you're all alive and there's nothing on the news about a rampaging pack of wild animals, so you seem to be in the clear. Or if you want to you can make a whole plot out of it, hangover style. The group can spend the rest of the session piecing together what they did and who they killed while they were raging. Very thematically appropriate to werewolf, if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:44:06-07:00","id":135521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135494#post135494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also point out that if the whole PC group goes into Basu-im, then you can just time skip forward.<br /> <br /> I think this was, in part, to address the issue at the start of the preview: one PC going into Kuruth and everyone else having to deal with it. If you can't stop them while in Wasu-im, while they are still in relative control and can contribute more effectively, then they go into Basu-im and drag everyone with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. It's not like you're supposed to be able to remember what happened, either. There's honestly no reason to play it out past the point the last PC goes Basu-Im. Just go, &quot;And that's it. Everyone is death raging; give me a few minutes to resolve and we'll wake you all up in Hishu and you can find out the consequences.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:48:49-07:00","id":135523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135510#post135510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, since you forget everything you did in Basu-Im anyway, you can cut to the pack waking up 12 hours later. If you don't want to deal with it beyond that, you can leave it at &quot;you don't know what happened, but you're all alive and there's nothing on the news about a rampaging pack of wild animals, so you seem to be in the clear. Or if you want to you can make a whole plot out of it, hangover style. The group can spend the rest of the session piecing together what they did and who they killed while they were raging. Very thematically appropriate to werewolf, if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd much rather give the players the option to play out the hunt, ideally with more control than auto-attack nearest thing. Unplanned loss of character agency does not, in my experience, lead to a happy group of players. Especially if it happens more than once.<br /> <br /> Put differently, if I'm promised a game of savage fury, I'd be a tad nonplussed if the storyteller takes my character away right when that fury arrives...<br /> <br /> (Note though, my group has proven on multiple occasions that I can rely on them to play out character breaks like Frenzy and Death Rage without them trying to game away the consequences. So I might be in the minority.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:48:50-07:00","id":135524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135443#post135443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not thrilled with the implication that non werewolf pack members are considered fair game in a mass frenzy though, what's the point of allowing wolfblooded and even muggles into a pack if they're just going to get murdered the first time their packmates lose their temper?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lest we forget, there's a reason they're called Forsaken. We all were asking how that little word carries on when the pack discussion came up-werewolves might be your cult/gang leaders, but they are something you fear as much as respect/reverence. Kuruth is the reason why.<br /> <br /> Also, the 'entire pack rages' thing puts the pack on a time limit, and they need to decide quick if they're going to try and fight their comrade or cut and run to minimize the damage. You only have so long to decide before the shit hits the fan. It's also a great moral question: Do you let your buddy go and hope the damage is minimal, or do you stick around and fight him out, with a very real probability that doing so could make everything worse? Tension and moral dubiousness is great stuff for stories. EDIT: It also does deal with the singular character focus-if one person loses time to Kuruth, there's a real shot everyone does.<br /> <br /> Finally, as for triggers, yeah, it depends on how that works out, but it provides more motive to struggle with Harmony, and triggers can be removed/added as convenient. I imagine the meat thing is more spirit side of the harmony divide than a human-I have trouble seeing Iron Masters, letting slip of their Harmony, becoming more of the wilderness recluses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-13-2014, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:08:00-07:00","id":135536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135523#post135523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'd much rather give the players the option to play out the hunt, ideally with more control than auto-attack nearest thing. Unplanned loss of character agency does not, in my experience, lead to a happy group of players. Especially if it happens more than once.</div> </div> </div> </div>This; yes. I'd feel cheated if the storyteller were to skip over these parts of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:14:39-07:00","id":135538,"title":"","content":"Very interesting with the new rules for Death Rage. My only real concern with all these new rules is that they may make it hard to play fo us who don't want big and heavy rulesets. But time will tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:35:25-07:00","id":135574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135510#post135510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, since you forget everything you did in Basu-Im anyway, you can cut to the pack waking up 12 hours later. If you don't want to deal with it beyond that, you can leave it at &quot;you don't know what happened, but you're all alive and there's nothing on the news about a rampaging pack of wild animals, so you seem to be in the clear. Or if you want to you can make a whole plot out of it, <b>hangover style</b>. The group can spend the rest of the session piecing together what they did and who they killed while they were raging. Very thematically appropriate to werewolf, if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>OMG! They really were a &quot;wolf pack&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:51:12-07:00","id":135607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135523#post135523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I'd much rather give the players the option to play out the hunt, ideally with more control than auto-attack nearest thing. Unplanned loss of character agency does not, in my experience, lead to a happy group of players. Especially if it happens more than once. Put differently, if I'm promised a game of savage fury, I'd be a tad nonplussed if the storyteller takes my character away right when that fury arrives... (Note though, my group has proven on multiple occasions that I can rely on them to play out character breaks like Frenzy and Death Rage without them trying to game away the consequences. So I might be in the minority.)</div> </div> </div> </div> That's fair, and I think there are times it's more appropriate to play it out and times it's more appropriate to time skip. Both can be interesting stories, it's just a matter of what the players will enjoy the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:59:02-07:00","id":135610,"title":"","content":"A climatic battle against the Pure.<br /> <br /> One of the player characters takes on the War Form.<br /> <br /> Due to simple bad luck, Death Rage overtakes her.<br /> <br /> She manages to kill one of the Pure's wolfblooded allies.<br /> <br /> Her packmates smell the kill and start Death Raging, too.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller ends the scene and skips to the next.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> No way. That's not how I run Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T12:06:31-07:00","id":135613,"title":"","content":"All I know is that both can be used in great effect by players and storytellers. Climatic battlescenes turning into rampaging bloodshed between the two packs, then there's the other side, where the PC's wake up and have to investigate why they're covered a little distance away from a Grocery Store massacre.<br /> <br /> I actually like the implications of being able to use it either way... also whoever is on the wrong side of a death raging werewolf is in some deep shit without silver haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T12:10:39-07:00","id":135616,"title":"","content":"And see, that would be a bad scene to do so in. Play it out-you have the rules to do so.<br /> <br /> But take that scene, and make it a Pure pack holding a bunch of humans and wolf blooded hostage, and one of them is slowly drawing their claws across a loved one's throat, digging deeper and deeper, and one of your pack leaps into Kuruth and kills someone, and then the pack all goes into Kuruth.<br /> <br /> It'd be very compelling, and terrifying, to skip that scene. Whose blood is on my hands, where are my packmates, and where is my beloved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T12:27:35-07:00","id":135656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135610#post135610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A climatic battle against the Pure. One of the player characters takes on the War Form. Due to simple bad luck, Death Rage overtakes her. She manages to kill one of the Pure's wolfblooded allies. Her packmates smell the kill and start Death Raging, too. The Storyteller ends the scene and skips to the next. --- No way. That's not how I run Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would be one if those times I mentioned where it's more appropriate to play it out. That said, I think there are times when a timeskip after Kuruth would make for an interesting story. That said, it is important to make sure the players are cool with that loss of agency. If they are not, that's another time it's more appropriate to play it out. It's just an option that's available to the storyteller, you can use it or not use it as suits the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T12:52:59-07:00","id":135672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135610#post135610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A climatic battle against the Pure.<br /> <br /> One of the player characters takes on the War Form.<br /> <br /> Due to simple bad luck, Death Rage overtakes her.<br /> <br /> She manages to kill one of the Pure's wolfblooded allies.<br /> <br /> Her packmates smell the kill and start Death Raging, too.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller ends the scene and skips to the next.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> No way. That's not how I run Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then by all means, play it out. If that's what you and your group prefer, then that's what you should do. Nobody's making you skip - I think the suggestion just came up in-thread as a potential story hook, nothing more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T12:55:11-07:00","id":135674,"title":"","content":"As the person that seemed to kick off this whole time-skip thing:<br /> <br /> There's a reason I said &quot;can&quot; and not, &quot;should&quot; or something similar. Nobody said, &quot;whenever the whole pack goes Basu-im just skip it because playing it out is stupid.&quot; There's no reason to be defensive about your group's style being one to play it out instead of skipping forward.<br /> <br /> Different people will want to handle it in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T13:11:20-07:00","id":135683,"title":"","content":"I hope it's a bit easier, by probability, for a harmonious wolf to avoid kuruth then it used to be. This is an upgrade from a thematic perspective but even more irritating to try to control for in play.<br /> <br /> I've never really liked kuruth though. The rage never fits into the story, as written, it just takes away your control of the character and either a) removes your ability to fight tactically versus dangerous opponents (this will at least be somewhat better now that gauru doesn't suck) or b) sends you careening into a murderous tangent. The math has ludicrous connotations, eventually. How do urban packs not inevitably slaughter a few dozen people per fiscal quarter? I'd like to play a dangerous beast, not an alcoholic serial killer.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite memories of playing wolf was the end of my character's blood talon initiation, where he was trapped in a grapple with his prey. She got stronger the more damage she took, to the point where he couldn't fight through the grapple without willpower (which he was out of) and he was running out of essence to keep healing. His vice was gluttony, so I asked the storyteller if I could use a WP to attack if he started eating the woman instead of just attacking her; they laughed and said yes. So he finished her off, and kept eating her, and failed his degeneration roll as he ran off into the night.<br /> <br /> It was a great twist for the character I'd never really anticipated, and he always knew that as much as he regretted it, he'd do it all over again if his back was to the wall. <i>That's </i>what I want kuruth to feel like - the choice to give in to a terrible rage inside to <i>do something </i>and achieve an end at grim cost, instead of occasionally losing all control because someone hit you hard or you smell blood. It's kind of interesting for deeply off-balance wolves to have weirder, longer raging, but for the harmonious it should be something more relevant to telling a story.<br /> <br /> The changes here took rage from being something irritating for a pack to manage to something impossible to manage meaningfully, without making it do anything more interesting or worthwhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":". 05-13-2014, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T13:13:00-07:00","id":135687,"title":"","content":"There's also the point that, as long as one player is still in control, it makes sense to play the scene. Imagine watching packmate after packmate fall to Kuruth while you're still struggling to keep your mind your own... and then they turn on you. That sounds like horror to me. That sounds like savage fury to me. Maybe you can't imagine fury unless you're the one in control of it? I don't know.<br /> <br /> The timeskip is a way to handle &quot;no one has any control anymore&quot;. If I were STing, I'd probably handle it by no longer describing anything and just asking for rolls. Some of the rolls would decide the next target; some would decide damage dealt; some would pick where you run off to when cooling off; etc. Successes might mean you followed a trail, or it might mean you found shelter instinctively, or it might mean nothing. Or maybe I wouldn't handle it that way; it seems like a lot to track for just re-creating the classical &quot;silent and black screen punctuated by horrible screams and roars and flashes of red claws&quot; scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T13:35:55-07:00","id":135719,"title":"","content":"Addressing Papa Bear's comment on the first page, that meat in the supermarket wouldn't really count as fresh meat. Recently slaughtered cattle that haven't been processed yet would be a different story, and no true Scots werewolf would be caught dead buying their meat from Stop and Shop. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm confident that'll be addressed either in the book or through an update. Glad I have time to save up for the deluxe hardcover version, no standard edition of this game for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T13:37:56-07:00","id":135720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135674#post135674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the person that seemed to kick off this whole time-skip thing:<br /> <br /> There's a reason I said &quot;can&quot; and not, &quot;should&quot; or something similar. Nobody said, &quot;whenever the whole pack goes Basu-im just skip it because playing it out is stupid.&quot; There's no reason to be defensive about your group's style being one to play it out instead of skipping forward.<br /> <br /> Different people will want to handle it in different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>To similarly clarify, my point was not at all intended to be &quot;time jump = bad&quot;. Rather that unplanned removal of player agency can be unpleasant, especially in excess. I had a DM who liked to do that once...it was not a great experience.<br /> <br /> Character memory holes can be fun, if the players are up for it. (Mummy: The Curse is prime territory for this as well)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T14:01:36-07:00","id":135736,"title":"","content":"Given that most of the rules for GMC are of the order of carrots rather than sticks (benefits for acting in a certain way, rather than prohibitions), I'd have preferred to see some kind of incentive system. I'd have liked to see the two types of Rage as conditions that would hand out Beats and Willpower liberally for violent behaviour. Ideally, I'd like to see something like the Murder XP system, but played dead serious. I want the game to congratulate and shower me with presents for raging... and then wake up 12 hours later in a house surrounded by the National Guard, a Gauru-sized hole in one wall and the blood of the family who lived there painting the walls.<br /> <br /> Ideally, I'd also like to see a penalty to holding an Uratha in the throes of Basu-Im back in any way. So if you are wrestling with them, or the like, you don't take a penalty, but if you are trying to hold them back so that they don't turn that little kid into Purina Wolf Chow, you should be taking penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T14:28:57-07:00","id":135752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135736#post135736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that most of the rules for GMC are of the order of carrots rather than sticks (benefits for acting in a certain way, rather than prohibitions), I'd have preferred to see some kind of incentive system. I'd have liked to see the two types of Rage as conditions that would hand out Beats and Willpower liberally for violent behaviour. Ideally, I'd like to see something like the Murder XP system, but played dead serious. I want the game to congratulate and shower me with presents for raging... and then wake up 12 hours later in a house surrounded by the National Guard, a Gauru-sized hole in one wall and the blood of the family who lived there painting the walls. Ideally, I'd also like to see a penalty to holding an Uratha in the throes of Basu-Im back in any way. So if you are wrestling with them, or the like, you don't take a penalty, but if you are trying to hold them back so that they don't turn that little kid into Purina Wolf Chow, you should be taking penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know, vampire Frenzy is also prohibitive - you can't take any action that doesn't directly contribute to getting what the Beast wants. It just happens that with werewolves, their &quot;Beast&quot; always wants to kill everything that moves. The carrot is that you get to spend more time in Gauru form, on the condition that you use the stick to beat what ever is closest to you to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T14:31:32-07:00","id":135754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135719#post135719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addressing Papa Bear's comment on the first page, that meat in the supermarket wouldn't really count as fresh meat. Recently slaughtered cattle that haven't been processed yet would be a different story, and no true Scots werewolf would be caught dead buying their meat from Stop and Shop. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm confident that'll be addressed either in the book or through an update. Glad I have time to save up for the deluxe hardcover version, no standard edition of this game for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on where you live. The town I went to college in had the slaughter house just outside the town limits. Directions to that town were &quot;north until you <i>smell </i>it, east until you step in it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 05-13-2014, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T14:56:35-07:00","id":135764,"title":"","content":"Ok, that was descriptive, eww.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T14:59:17-07:00","id":135765,"title":"","content":"Have any of you tried playing out these new rules using one of the demos or premade game systems? I'm curious as to your results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:04:32-07:00","id":135772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135765#post135765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have any of you tried playing out these new rules using one of the demos or premade game systems? I'm curious as to your results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gimme until Friday. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:15:38-07:00","id":135813,"title":"","content":"Apparently no, first draft doesn't has any way to stop the Wasu-Im from eventually becoming Basu-Im. Triggers also seem like they'll be customizable. I'm wondering now: What happened with the term Kuruth?<br /> <br /> Second drafts they're looking at providing a merit to restrain Wasu-Im before you explode into Basu-Im, not very elegant IMO. A single packmate who kills in Basu still fucks your psych over.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pitch: Maybe totems help werewolves from reaching Basu-Im, not automatically, roll something. It gives you an incentive to be in a pack and, it\u2019s better than trying to fix it with a merit because one stray packmate who goes Basu and kills something fucks you sideways anyway.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:21:02-07:00","id":135822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135764#post135764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that was descriptive, eww.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've got the new sub-title for the Idigam Chronicles: Blood &amp; Eww. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T16:22:26-07:00","id":135865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135356#post135356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like I might be in the minority here, but I'm not liking what I am seeing here. If the smell of fresh meat can set them off, then they can't even walk thru the butcher's section of the grocery store without losing it. It pushes the werewolves into being reclusive, woods-dwellers who can't ever go near civilization.<br /> <br /> Like so many other things, I need to see it in play. Without the Harmony scale, it's hard to gauge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I am looking at it right now, is if that level of Kuruth trigger is way down on the spirit/wolf side, then your character is probably hunting his beef anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T16:44:10-07:00","id":135879,"title":"","content":"Once your at that point of spirit wolfitude you're stuck in the hisil anyway. You pretty much become an unihar by the looks of it. <br /> <br /> Also for play test I mean ALL the spoilers, not just the kuruth one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T16:54:04-07:00","id":135884,"title":"","content":"Seems like just a few months ago some people thought a big drawback of Werewolf was it didn't resemble the movies where people black out and wake up after having killed a bunch of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T16:57:03-07:00","id":135885,"title":"","content":"That's why i was shocked by the garou form complaints. Glad so far Stew isn't changing that up too much. Did i see him say its now the higher of wits or dex? I usually have either of those stats around a 2 anyway x.x","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T17:39:21-07:00","id":135953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135884#post135884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like just a few months ago some people thought a big drawback of Werewolf was it didn't resemble the movies where people black out and wake up after having killed a bunch of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was never one of those people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T18:07:22-07:00","id":135960,"title":"","content":"My complaint is that from the first draft of things, it's gone too far in the other direction, and made it not-fun. I'm all well and good with the idea of synchronized gory demolition crew, but there should at least be a chance to defuse that bomb with the Soft Rage starts, or possibly even force Death Rage to end (with appropriate Merits - maybe Fighting Style: Berserk for those Uratha who learn to tame and thus weaponize Kuruth). I'm not saying that shouldn't be risky (the choice to go out into the woods and instead mutilate some unfortunate deer or seal yourself in the Shadow for the duration should be viable options too), but if a player does do that, they're out of the game until Kuruth times out, they're just not going to hurt anyone they care about. Scene-skip doesn't work if the Basu-Immir never gets a chance to provoke infectious rage (and again, after the unavoidable third episode of that, it gets aggravating instead of interesting; &quot;Ugh, another trigger. Who did I kill this time, oh brother...&quot;).<br /> <br /> So, Touchstones giving you a wake up call (I don't know the IC reason, maybe the kinship of the Touchstone soothes the genetic memory of Father Wolf and reminds him that the Forsaken are indeed carrying on his legacy of protecting the world) seems sensible. And suitably risky, because if it <i>doesn't work, </i>they get Super Gauru for their trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 05-13-2014, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T18:09:49-07:00","id":135962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135884#post135884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like just a few months ago some people thought a big drawback of Werewolf was it didn't resemble the movies where people black out and wake up after having killed a bunch of people.</div> </div> </div> </div> Indeed, I certainly made statements to that effect. And I am thrilled with the sound of new Kuruth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T18:36:49-07:00","id":136002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=135884#post135884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like just a few months ago some people thought a big drawback of Werewolf was it didn't resemble the movies where people black out and wake up after having killed a bunch of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was gonna say, isn't this why people loved the Cursed so much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T19:23:29-07:00","id":136079,"title":"","content":"At least with Vampire Frenzy you can say &quot;the Beast wants X&quot; and work towards it, rather than just &quot;kill everything in range&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, it's &quot;until killed&quot; so there's no more &quot;knocking the target out and moving on&quot;, or &quot;playing dead&quot; it seems (which clarifies from WtF rules which just say attack, and doesn't talk about &quot;until death&quot; or &quot;until not moving&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T19:39:47-07:00","id":136114,"title":"","content":"Kuruth is to Werewolf what Blood is to Vampire, from a certain thematic viewpoint. Of course it needs to be harsher than Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T20:09:16-07:00","id":136141,"title":"","content":"I certainly agree that there should be any number of Kuruth dampeners; talking down the about-to-mindlessly-rampage beast is practically a trope in and of itself. I actually wonder if the Social Manuevering system can be shoehorned in, simply by severely compacting the time-per-roll to 1 turn, 2 turns, 5 turns, 10 turns and removing hard leverage as an option. You'd pretty much need perfection to talk down a Harmony 1/10 Wasu-Im, but even a stranger could manage a Harmony 5 werewolf with a bit of luck. I'd also consider throwing in Animal Ken as a bonus to rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T20:22:53-07:00","id":136149,"title":"","content":"Also, I never said: Tilts are going to be in the book! Happy dance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T20:34:25-07:00","id":136154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=136149#post136149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I never said: Tilts are going to be in the book! Happy dance!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, now I wanna know which facility Urshul gets to inflict them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T21:45:53-07:00","id":136188,"title":"","content":"Yeah I don't want to see &quot;talking down the monster&quot; scenes or anything like that; it should just be an Elodoth gift for outside influence, imo. Otherwise I'd consider that &quot;manipulating&quot; which now gets Primal Urge in penalty dice...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:02:43-07:00","id":136255,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that Wasu-im is a 2 stage limit, then you fly into direct Kuruth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T07:29:33-07:00","id":136654,"title":"","content":"I do like the two stages, a soft rage and a hard rage, I would just like to see a way to avoid the hard rage. Or being able to voluntarily soft rage to avoid a hard rage when you need to keep some control.<br /> <br /> This would make it difficult to hunt spirits of rage and anger, since they could just use Influence to send Uratha into Kuruth and fall back to not be the nearest target, and watch a pack destroy itself on the hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:52:52-07:00","id":136782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=136654#post136654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the two stages, a soft rage and a hard rage, I would just like to see a way to avoid the hard rage. Or being able to voluntarily soft rage to avoid a hard rage when you need to keep some control.<br /> <br /> This would make it difficult to hunt spirits of rage and anger, since they could just use Influence to send Uratha into Kuruth and fall back to not be the nearest target, and watch a pack destroy itself on the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a ritual defining the target of the hunt could give you a (very hard) resolve + composure roll each time you want to attack the target of the hunt instead of the closest target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:27:49-07:00","id":136803,"title":"","content":"Remember flying off the handle is an extremes situation. A properly grounded uratha would only kuruth at a rape or child abuse, or some other emotional trigger. It's the loose cannons that go off for nothing. By that point I'm sure a Blood Talon lodge of hunting such peoples has already noticed them and worked to dispatch em.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:50:26-07:00","id":136820,"title":"","content":"I like this trigger: Being injured by silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:30:10-07:00","id":136868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=136820#post136820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this trigger: Being injured by silver.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. That should remain a trigger at any Harmony level, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T11:25:06-07:00","id":136917,"title":"","content":"Something I'd really like to see if how the Kuruth triggers in the extremes mimic what the uratha is ignoring. Say the human-focused HAS to change during the full moon, gets angry the fresher meat he sees,etc. His wolf desperately to come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:22:22-07:00","id":136969,"title":"","content":"Ana I love your posts. I'm sure that's the situation though. And wasn't damage by silver always a kuruth risk? I know Aggro damage is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:38:08-07:00","id":137016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=136969#post136969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ana I love your posts. I'm sure that's the situation though. And wasn't damage by silver always a kuruth risk? I know Aggro damage is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they're customizable here, think of how vampires go accumulating Banes as they drop humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T13:04:53-07:00","id":137057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=136969#post136969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ana I love your posts. I'm sure that's the situation though. And wasn't damage by silver always a kuruth risk? I know Aggro damage is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you ^^<br /> <br /> Well, I think there are always some basic Kuruth risks that all Uratha share. It just makes sense they would, so silver and agg sound pretty good.<br /> <br /> I don't feel this Kuruth change is all that bad. But one thing that sticks out to me is the mass Kuruth. Now, I like the idea, but it will be a game killer in online games (games with 30+ players and status quo of some sort). One might say that the game isn't meant to be played that way, but a lot of great WoD memories have come from these online games for a reason. Anyway, having a 30 person brawl with wolf-blooded in the middle may be a fun idea, but it hurts the game severly. I think there should be a way for the others to go into soft-rage before hard-rage, like in normal Kuruth. That way, these larger game killer brawls could be avoided.<br /> <br /> And to note a previous point. It doesn't really feel as satifying to end a siege against Pure in a massive death rage brawl. In those situations, strategy is much more in the forefront.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T18:50:54-07:00","id":137477,"title":"","content":"I guess it's unclear to me how forgiving triggers are in the Harmony 4-6 range. That has a significant impact on how this plays out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T19:49:17-07:00","id":137632,"title":"","content":"How can it be clear how forgiving/unforgiving the enitre thing is? We only have the general idea laid out before us. We have <i>literally</i> nothing to judge off of other than metaphorical fog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T22:37:11-07:00","id":137745,"title":"","content":"I think the triggers for the in balance harmony are not 'forgiving' persay, but dramatic. <br /> <br /> It'll take a lot of someone whose collected to lose their cool. Walking by the parking garage at the college and seeing a woman get assaulted by 5 guys would probably be the things (but a simple wasu-im might solve that). <br /> <br /> Again we're looking at extremes for unforgiving triggers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T00:13:10-07:00","id":137852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=137057#post137057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel this Kuruth change is all that bad. But one thing that sticks out to me is the mass Kuruth. Now, I like the idea, but it will be a game killer in online games (games with 30+ players and status quo of some sort). One might say that the game isn't meant to be played that way, but a lot of great WoD memories have come from these online games for a reason. Anyway, having a 30 person brawl with wolf-blooded in the middle may be a fun idea, but it hurts the game severly. I think there should be a way for the others to go into soft-rage before hard-rage, like in normal Kuruth. That way, these larger game killer brawls could be avoided.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Online is my primary game venue, so I'm totally understanding that aspect. But I like the infectious idea even with that in mind. That's also why I want to know if there are other ways to bring them out or if they just rage around for however long they're required to stay in rage mode; a 12 hour Kuruth fest would level small to medium sized towns, let alone the trouble in a bigger city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T01:46:30-07:00","id":137901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=137852#post137852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Online is my primary game venue, so I'm totally understanding that aspect. But I like the infectious idea even with that in mind. That's also why I want to know if there are other ways to bring them out or if they just rage around for however long they're required to stay in rage mode; a 12 hour Kuruth fest would level small to medium sized towns, let alone the trouble in a bigger city.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea as well, don't get me wrong. But I just feel it might be houseruled away in online games because its going to cause problems when new people enter the room in the chat where the scene is happening. Plus, again, 30+ wolf brawl XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:00:30-07:00","id":138103,"title":"","content":"There is a maximum range for infectious Kuruth. Just say the newcomer was standing far enough away when the triggering kill was scored that he didn't smell the kill and now he's watching this 30 gauru murderfest from a relatively safe distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:45:13-07:00","id":138158,"title":"","content":"Don't you have to be in the same pack as the wolf that fell into Kuruth for the Basu-Im infection to occur?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:55:35-07:00","id":138165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devil bunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=138158#post138158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you have to be in the same pack as the wolf that fell into Kuruth for the Basu-Im infection to occur?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, and members of the same pack who are in Death Rage together do not attack each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:45:09-07:00","id":138414,"title":"","content":"For the unlucky Wolf-Blooded standing next to the Kuruth guy:<br /> Can\u00b4t there be a Rite or a Totem that makes Wolf-Blooded part of the Hunting Party and thus put them out of the target lock ?<br /> <br /> What\u00b4s really tough about Kuruth is, it also makes Battle Plans or Pack Tactics nonexistent.<br /> Like: &quot;You and George sneak in from the back door, Pete cuts off their escape route and by then someone<br /> will most likely loose it so we will all go batshit and hope for the best.&quot;<br /> Or is Kuruth totally independant from combat situations ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, will this Kuruth lead to a sort of mutual &quot;kuruthal deterrence&quot; between Pure and Forsaken ?<br /> Because going at each other throats could mean that a lone wolf wakes up in the heap of two dead Packs with<br /> no idea what happened ?<br /> <br /> Will Elodoth have a new role ? Skirmishing the edge of the battle, watching for Mates about to loose it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1261,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","user":"Doc Lumbago","date":". 05-15-2014, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:05:25-07:00","id":138639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=137901#post137901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the idea as well, don't get me wrong. But I just feel it might be houseruled away in online games because its going to cause problems when new people enter the room in the chat where the scene is happening. Plus, again, 30+ wolf brawl XD</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically what happened with Predator's Taint in VtR. &quot;I know we set up this intricate Court scene, but the new vampires who want to introduce themselves to the Prince and 5 of the Primogen all failed their Predator's Taint check, so the scene is scrapped for a 5 hour combat scene. Yay. :/ &quot;<br /> <br /> Everything about Kuruth is fine, even for bigger games (on and offline) as long as there's a way to end it early or prevent it from going full bore all the time rather than a mandatory &quot;you get 2 turns of soft rage and then everyone goes death rage regardless.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T22:24:15-07:00","id":138951,"title":"","content":"By running yesterday first game session of my Wolf-Blooded game I realize something. New &quot;infectious&quot; Death Rage rules make much more sense in games where couple of characters are one by one having First Change. Group of mortals on verge of Change are making, unconsciously, they own pack and each First Change - connected with at least <i>Wasu-Im</i> - triggers building up Rage in next one, leading to his First Change. It's like domino effect, very nice looking in game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T01:12:11-07:00","id":139106,"title":"","content":"For me, this is really going to depend on the exact triggers. Death Rage itself seems to be overly harsh, which while I find appropriate in a way, I feel that it shouldn't be something triggered every other scene, especially not with its infectious nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:45:03-07:00","id":139256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=138951#post138951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By running yesterday first game session of my Wolf-Blooded game I realize something. New &quot;infectious&quot; Death Rage rules make much more sense in games where couple of characters are one by one having First Change. Group of mortals on verge of Change are making, unconsciously, they own pack and each First Change - connected with at least <i>Wasu-Im</i> - triggers building up Rage in next one, leading to his First Change. It's like domino effect, very nice looking in game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that wind up creating a whole pack of one Auspice, since they're going thru the First Change so close together? Even a week apart would only allow Rahu to Cahalith to Elodoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:49:54-07:00","id":139262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=139256#post139256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't that wind up creating a whole pack of one Auspice, since they're going thru the First Change so close together? Even a week apart would only allow Rahu to Cahalith to Elodoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh good god.. I can just imagine it. A pack with 6 Rahus in it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T07:58:31-07:00","id":139328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=139256#post139256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that wind up creating a whole pack of one Auspice, since they're going thru the First Change so close together? Even a week apart would only allow Rahu to Cahalith to Elodoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you mean that in time of one week you could get 3 difference Auspices. See this lunar calendar we use in our game - <a href=\"http://www.calendar-365.com/moon-calendar/2014/January.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.calendar-365.com/moon-cal...4/January.html</a> - every Auspice have 2 times a month 3 consecutive nights, except Rahu that has one week. I don't make that whole pack is changing each other night, for 5 days in month. Just it looks logical that building up Rage before First Change in one, leads to building up Rage in another pack member. And Death Rage of first in time of First Change leads to investigating things finally leading to uncover nature of Uratha - like dead deers, weird sleepwalking or shapechanging.<br /> <br /> We started with half conscious change of our <i>Irraka</i> on 1st of January. Two days investigation leads to now <i>Ithaeur</i> First Change when he was confronted with other werewolf and is now on edge of life and death on 4th. Our Rahu will need to wait most - because of week in game time - but will all that is going on, he could logically just take next phase in next 2-3 days. It's a domino effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-16-2014, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:37:33-07:00","id":139346,"title":"","content":"See as for the pack tactics complaint, Doc, it really isn't a problem if your pack keeps their shit together. I.E. maintain harmony.<br /> <br /> If your pack is so far gone that they expect someone to lose their shit from an adrenaline burst then your pack is most likely not going to be all that organized anyway. More like a pack of savage animals or super accountants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T18:54:13-07:00","id":167421,"title":"","content":"So after reading, re-reading, a re-reading the new Death Rage stuff, I don't like it. <br /> <br /> Oh you're pack wants to do a stealthy hunt so lets attack during the new moon. Oh no your Irraka isn't perfectly balanced so by being out side she's automatically forced into soft rage, which has no choice but to go into death rage, which leads to the entire pack death raging and getting nothing accomplished. <br /> <br /> Why would any werewolf pack ever hunt at night then when it will lead to your entire pack Death raging 100% of the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3282-a-bigger-blacker-dick","name":"A Bigger Blacker Dick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:02:19-07:00","id":167423,"title":"","content":"Because most would find ways to deal with it and night's still a good time to run people down?<br /> <br /> It's not as harsh as you think, and fluxing into a more stable Harmony is easier than expected. It's enough to be a challenge and to cause a question of whether you keep the pack together or not, but not enough to screw you completely over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T23:39:08-07:00","id":167650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bigger Blacker Dick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=167421#post167421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh you're pack wants to do a stealthy hunt so lets attack during the new moon. Oh no your Irraka isn't perfectly balanced so by being out side she's automatically forced into soft rage, which has no choice but to go into death rage, which leads to the entire pack death raging and getting nothing accomplished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soft Rage don't end every time with Hard Rage - you can choose targets, but can also use your Resolve+Composure to calm down, it's just much harder. And Soft Rager can just flee the scene, seeing he could be dangerous to the pack.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T00:14:10-07:00","id":167661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bigger Blacker Dick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=167421#post167421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So after reading, re-reading, a re-reading the new Death Rage stuff, I don't like it.<br /> <br /> Oh you're pack wants to do a stealthy hunt so lets attack during the new moon. Oh no your Irraka isn't perfectly balanced so by being out side she's automatically forced into soft rage, which has no choice but to go into death rage, which leads to the entire pack death raging and getting nothing accomplished.<br /> <br /> Why would any werewolf pack ever hunt at night then when it will lead to your entire pack Death raging 100% of the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason why you'd let your Irraka get so unbalanced that he death rages all the time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T06:22:49-07:00","id":167823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=167661#post167661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same reason why you'd let your Irraka get so unbalanced that he death rages all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>But according to what was posted it doesn't take an unbalanced werewolf to death rage under his moon. It takes a mid point werewolf. One who is not 100% perfectly aligned with harmony. It's not unreasonable to think that the every day struggles of being a Forsaken takes it's toll on the soul. Very few werewolves are 100% perfectly balanced. It's being on par with the Dali Lama.<br /> <br /> I just find it odd that now a werewolves auspice moon is a weakness. Something for them to fear and hide from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3282-a-bigger-blacker-dick","name":"A Bigger Blacker Dick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T11:56:58-07:00","id":168131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bigger Blacker Dick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=167823#post167823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But according to what was posted it doesn't take an unbalanced werewolf to death rage under his moon. It takes a mid point werewolf. One who is not 100% perfectly aligned with harmony. It's not unreasonable to think that the every day struggles of being a Forsaken takes it's toll on the soul. Very few werewolves are 100% perfectly balanced. It's being on par with the Dali Lama.</div> </div> </div> </div>So when you get unbalanced <i>stop and rebalance</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T12:15:12-07:00","id":168187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bigger Blacker Dick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=167823#post167823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just find it odd that now a werewolves auspice moon is a weakness. Something for them to fear and hide from.</div> </div> </div> </div> Odd? It was odd before when that wasn't the case. now it's finally in line with like 90% of werewolf lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T12:20:11-07:00","id":168197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=167650#post167650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Soft Rage don't end every time with Hard Rage - you can choose targets, but can also use your Resolve+Composure to calm down, it's just much harder. And Soft Rager can just flee the scene, seeing he could be dangerous to the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually it does. Of you re-read the blog entry carefully, you'll notice that success on the Resolve + Composure roll doesn't end the rage, it just gives you one more interval in Soft Rage. After the second interval you go full on Death Rage no matter what. It just buys you more time to get away from anyone you don't want to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T13:03:20-07:00","id":168221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=168187#post168187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Odd? It was odd before when that wasn't the case. now it's finally in line with like 90% of werewolf lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Werewolf Lore deals primarily with the Full Moon, I have to agree that it is Odd that any moon has this effect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T13:11:25-07:00","id":168227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=168221#post168221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that Werewolf Lore deals primarily with the Full Moon, I have to agree that it is Odd that any moon has this effect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but if you're going to have werewolves with affinities for different lunar phases, you would think they'd be affected in this way by the phase they're associated with, rather than all having the same reaction to the full moon regardless of Auspice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T14:08:46-07:00","id":168247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=168227#post168227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, but if you're going to have werewolves with affinities for different lunar phases, you would think they'd be affected in this way by the phase they're associated with, rather than all having the same reaction to the full moon regardless of Auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a fair point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Though I like much of where Idigam is going, I do not actually like Kuruth in the new system. Not sure exactly why that is, but something about it just rubs me wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T14:22:22-07:00","id":168250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=168247#post168247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also a fair point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Though I like much of where Idigam is going, I do not actually like Kuruth in the new system. Not sure exactly why that is, but something about it just rubs me wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's reasonable. I myself am not 100% sold on it. I really like the auspice moon as a potential triggering criteria depending on Harmony, but that's more an aspect of Harmony than Kuruth. I like the soft rage vs. full rage as well. But I'm a little iffy on the fact that once you soft rage you're going to death rage, and it's just a matter of how long. I'm also not convinced on the whole pack raging... I get that it's to avoid the &quot;tie him down until he's calm&quot; solution, but I'll have to see it in play before I know if &quot;everyone death rages&quot; is any better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T18:28:03-07:00","id":169388,"title":"","content":"In the first edition, you risked kuruth just by getting five successes on an attack roll (or being on the receiving end of the same). Hands-down the kuruth roll I've made the most. Those attacks might be a bit rarer with GMC combat, but that still being a trigger in the Harmony 4-6 range would make the new kuruth incredibly aggravating, even with the chain rage rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T01:53:47-07:00","id":169623,"title":"","content":"Yesterday we had first Death Rage scene in play and I'm a bit dissatisfied. Only things what Kuruth rules do in general is &quot;ST is taking your character control&quot;. No &quot;werewolf become unstable beast&quot; or &quot;he is one to fight everyone&quot;. Also, new rules emphases pack should follow after one Uratha in Death Rage - but this is after he kills someone. What if there isn't any kill, but Kuruth is full on?<br /> <br /> And last but not least - character is taking Gauru form to combat, his conciseness decision. Is he already in <i>Basu-Im</i>? He roll each round on his Resolve+Composure -2? There must pass Primal Urge rounds? Is player controlling character or not? Spoiler is very vague on it's wording and with that a bit confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T07:23:43-07:00","id":169769,"title":"","content":"If you Death-Rage and don't manage to kill anything for its whole duration? No, the rest of the pack would not rage. As for taking Gauru form in combat, that doesn't automatically make you rage. You only risk it if you don't attack or move towards the nearest enemy. If you take Gauru form out of combat (though I can't imagine why you would want to), you automatically Death-Rage. It's not clear wether either circumstance triggers Wasu-Im or Basu-Im, but my assumption for now is that you always start out in soft rage, regardless of the trigger. Also, the ST does not have to take control of a Death-Raging character. Just like the ST doesn't have to take control of a Frenzying vampire character. Just inform the player that they must spend every action attempting to attack or move towards the nearest enemy, and let them make all other decisions for their character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:15:41-07:00","id":170757,"title":"","content":"Something else I immediately dislike - Instant fall into Death Rage in Garou out of Combat. I think it is very thematic to start resisting the Death Rage (making the roll for not attacking/moving to attack), and you may even be at a penalty greater than normal (greater than the -2 normally associates with Garou Form), but Instantly falling to Kuruth just irritates me. It eliminates some cool posturing, if you are willing to take the risk. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:39:13-07:00","id":170778,"title":"","content":"Remember that you're just seeing the core info around Kuruth in what Stew revealed. IC comes in a whole package of areas of game that overlap and affect one another. There will be the space you want for posturing in there, just wait and see what form it takes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:44:14-07:00","id":170781,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I know we are lacking... But for argument sake... I LIKE using my Garou Form to Posture (Cahalith War Howler). It comes with Risks. In Idigam, using Garou to do so appears to be an immediate path to Kuruth (You are out of Combat and in Garou - So Kuruth). I don't like &quot;Immediate paths&quot; to such things. I prefer &quot;Resistant paths.&quot; That is all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still - Much of the revealed stuff is interesting. Looking forward to seeing more.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:47:37-07:00","id":170782,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I can't really reveal any more about said posturing at this stage because Stew and the NDA Ninjas would probably do horrible things to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:48:57-07:00","id":170783,"title":"","content":"Gotta love the Ninja's. I set traps for them. Sadly, I rarely catch any, they be sneaksy and tricksy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T21:32:10-07:00","id":171393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135189-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-kuruth?p=170781#post170781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know we are lacking... But for argument sake... I LIKE using my Garou Form to Posture (Cahalith War Howler). It comes with Risks. In Idigam, using Garou to do so appears to be an immediate path to Kuruth (You are out of Combat and in Garou - So Kuruth). I don't like &quot;Immediate paths&quot; to such things. I prefer &quot;Resistant paths.&quot; That is all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still - Much of the revealed stuff is interesting. Looking forward to seeing more.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Dalu was how you were supposed to do posturing. Or is that just pre-Idigam I-use-Dalu-for-everything-anyways-so-it's-not-special-anymore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T20:55:34-07:00","id":172343,"title":"","content":"So I just realized something. A lot of Kuruth triggers have to do with the character's Auspice moon, right? Depending on how balanced your Harmony is, that can mean any time your Auspice moon even rises, or only when you look directly at it, or only when you see your own reflection with your Auspice moon behind it... So... How's that going to work with the Pure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","e